Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• state_name / state_code : identify California records ( `state_name = 'California'` or `state_code = '06'` )  
• date_local       : filter to the 2020 calendar year and extract month (`EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local)`)  
• arithmetic_mean    : daily mean concentration that will be averaged to a monthly mean  
• parameter_name    : quick inspection to be sure we are pulling the intended pollutant  
• units_of_measure    : sanity‑check that the same units are used inside one pollutant table  
• Other descriptive columns (city_name, latitude …) are useful only for ad‑hoc checks and are not needed in the final aggregation  

Per‑table conditions  

1. `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`  – PM10  
2. `…pm25_frm_daily_summary`           – PM2.5 FRM  
3. `…pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary`         – PM2.5 non‑FRM  
4. `…voc_daily_summary`             – VOC (volatile organic compounds)  
5. `…so2_daily_summary`             – SO₂ ( result will be *10 )  
6. `…lead_daily_summary`            – Lead ( result will be *100 )  

All queries will look only at California (`state_code = '06'` or `state_name = 'California'`) and `date_local` in 2020.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
