Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and how they will be used  

• state_name / state_code : identify California records ( `state_name = 'California'` or `state_code = '06'` )  
• date_local       : filter to the 2020 calendar year and extract month (`EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local)`)  
• arithmetic_mean    : daily mean concentration that will be averaged to a monthly mean  
• parameter_name    : quick inspection to be sure we are pulling the intended pollutant  
• units_of_measure    : sanity‑check that the same units are used inside one pollutant table  
• Other descriptive columns (city_name, latitude …) are useful only for ad‑hoc checks and are not needed in the final aggregation  

Per‑table conditions  

1. `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`  – PM10  
2. `…pm25_frm_daily_summary`           – PM2.5 FRM  
3. `…pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary`         – PM2.5 non‑FRM  
4. `…voc_daily_summary`             – VOC (volatile organic compounds)  
5. `…so2_daily_summary`             – SO₂ ( result will be *10 )  
6. `…lead_daily_summary`            – Lead ( result will be *100 )  

All queries will look only at California (`state_code = '06'` or `state_name = 'California'`) and `date_local` in 2020.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
10 exploratory‑to‑final SQL statements
-------------------------------------------------------------------

```sql
-- 1. Description: List the distinct state_name values in the PM10 table to confirm the naming convention.
SELECT DISTINCT state_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Description: Show the distinct PM10 parameter names used in California during 2020.
SELECT DISTINCT parameter_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Description: Sample daily PM10 data for California in January 2020.
SELECT date_local, county_name, arithmetic_mean
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND date_local BETWEEN '2020-01-01' AND '2020-01-31'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Description: Inspect PM2.5‑FRM parameter names recorded in California in 2020.
SELECT DISTINCT parameter_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_frm_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Description: Sample VOC records for California (any month of 2020).
SELECT date_local, arithmetic_mean, units_of_measure
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.voc_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Description: Retrieve daily SO2 means for Los Angeles County in 2020 to inspect the magnitude.
SELECT date_local, county_name, arithmetic_mean
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.so2_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND county_name = 'Los Angeles'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Description: Show Lead parameter names used in California (2020) to be sure scaling applies to Pb only.
SELECT DISTINCT parameter_name
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.lead_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Description: Compute monthly average PM10 for CA in 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS pm10_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Description: Compute monthly average PM2.5 (non‑FRM) for CA in 2020.
SELECT
  EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month,
  AVG(arithmetic_mean)           AS pm25_nonfrm_avg
FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary`
WHERE state_code = '06'
  AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
GROUP BY month
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Description: Final query – monthly averages of all requested pollutants in California for 2020,
--                  scaling SO2 by 10 and Lead by 100.
SELECT
  m12.month,
  pm10_avg,
  pm25_frm_avg,
  pm25_nonfrm_avg,
  voc_avg,
  so2_avg * 10    AS so2_avg_scaled,
  lead_avg * 100  AS lead_avg_scaled
FROM (
  -- PM10
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS pm10_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm10_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m1
FULL JOIN (
  -- PM2.5 FRM
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS pm25_frm_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_frm_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m2 USING (month)
FULL JOIN (
  -- PM2.5 non‑FRM
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS pm25_nonfrm_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.pm25_nonfrm_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m3 USING (month)
FULL JOIN (
  -- VOC
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS voc_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.voc_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m4 USING (month)
FULL JOIN (
  -- SO2
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS so2_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.so2_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m5 USING (month)
FULL JOIN (
  -- Lead
  SELECT EXTRACT(MONTH FROM date_local) AS month, AVG(arithmetic_mean) AS lead_avg
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.epa_historical_air_quality.lead_daily_summary`
  WHERE state_code = '06' AND EXTRACT(YEAR FROM date_local) = 2020
  GROUP BY month
) AS m6 USING (month)
ORDER BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

